{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/163581-the-sea-of-shadows-prior-3rd-maelstrom","id":163581,"title":"The Sea of shadows prior 3rd Maelstrom","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Wraith: The Oblivion"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-06-09T07:51:51-07:00","id":163581,"title":"The Sea of shadows prior 3rd Maelstrom","content":"What would be the dangers of entering/falling or navigating the Sea of Shadows prior the 3rd Maelstom? Also, a vampire that could fall into the Sea of Shadows would suffer what kind of pain/damage (mentally and physically)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3082-dfcastro","name":"dfcastro","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3082_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-10T08:22:52-07:00","id":164846,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><i><b>\u201c\u2026is the area that lies between the Shadowlands and the rest of the Underworld and surrounds all of the inner realms, the place which used to be simply known as the Darkness. Though devoid of light, it was not filled with storms and wild chaotic beings and places until it became saturated with them all by the Third Great Maelstrom,\u201d</b></i> (<i>The Sea of Shadows</i>, p. 23).<br /> <br /> I imagine the tone being similar to <i>The Road</i> \u2013 creepy and desolate. Or. Did you ever see <i>Insidious</i>? Remember when the father went out into the \u201cFurther\u201d [because, apparently, that\u2019s the best name writers could come up with\u2026] to look for his kid? That\u2019s kinda how I\u2019d imagine it. More creepy, less grabby. <br /> <br /> Vampires: I\u2019d probably use the same mechanics for Wraiths. I imagine, like honey badgers, the Tempest doesn\u2019t care if you\u2019re dead or undead. Maybe the Tah Lah Lah [sic] has some nifty Argos-like Necromancy\u2026 </span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:8px\"><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">&lt;signature&gt; something witty &lt;/signature&gt;</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/302-nazfool","name":"Nazfool","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar302_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"753"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-11T17:08:06-07:00","id":166362,"title":"","content":"Nazfool, I appreciate the content added by you, but it seems to be a little misplaced because this description fits to a Sea of Shadows after the Third Maelstrom.<br /> The problem is that I have some players that entered in the Shadowlands and they are in Haiti in the same time as the first spanish ships arrived. So it is before the Thirsd Maelstrom and also near Dark Kingdom of Obsidian.<br /> <br /> Then my assumption, it can be wrong, is that those Dark Kingdoms are islands separated by a Sea or Ocean. Then what is that Sea?<br /> - The Sea of Shadow that will become the Tempest.<br /> - The Sunless Sea?<br /> - The Open Sea?<br /> <br /> I do not know what sea was permanently disturbed by the Third Maelstrom and became the Tempest that we now know.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3082-dfcastro","name":"dfcastro","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3082_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-12T11:04:15-07:00","id":167082,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:courier new, courier, monospace\">Before it became the Tempest (before the 3</span><sup>rd</sup><span style=\"font-family:courier new, courier, monospace\"> GM) it was called the Darkness. After the 3</span><sup>rd</sup><span style=\"font-family:courier new, courier, monospace\"> GM, it became the Tempest.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:courier new, courier, monospace\">According to </span><i>The Sea of Shadows</i><span style=\"font-family:courier new, courier, monospace\"> (1995):</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:courier new, courier, monospace\">The Tempest is located \u201cbetween\u201d the Shadowlands and the rest of the Underworld.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:courier new, courier, monospace\">The Sunless Sea is \u201cbetween\u201d Stygia (and, by extension, the other Dark Kingdoms probably) and the Far Shores.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:courier new, courier, monospace\">The Sea of Souls is, to my understanding, an artificial construct created after the 1</span><sup>st</sup><span style=\"font-family:courier new, courier, monospace\"> GM that creates a border for an area of the Sunless Sea claimed by Stygia. Weeping Bay is part of the Sea of Souls.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:courier new, courier, monospace\">The Sea of Shadows is \u201cbetween\u201d Stygia (et al) and the Labyrinth. </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:courier new, courier, monospace\">Open Sea is \u201cafter/outward\u201d from Stygia (et al) but not moving \u201ctowards\u201d the Labyrinth or the Shadowlands.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:courier new, courier, monospace\">In nomenclature, \u201cThe Tempest\u201d is used to describe all areas of \u201cspace between places.\u201d For example, while the Tempest proper is between the Shadowlands and the rest of the Underworld, it would not be uncommon to hear a Harbinger talk about navigating the Tempest in the Sea of Souls. </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:courier new, courier, monospace\">So, players in the Shadowlands of Haiti in (I\u2019m guessing) the late 15</span><sup>th</sup><span style=\"font-family:courier new, courier, monospace\"> century probably wouldn't need to worry about the \u201cDarkness\u201d so long as they\u2019re sticking to the Shadowlands. If they want to journey towards the Underworld, they\u2019d have to negotiate the aforementioned Darkness. </span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:courier new, courier, monospace\">[This is my interpretation of the Underworld\u2019s necrography. Many troupes will have different interpretations. Personally, I always like these disagreements because I imagine (IC) wraiths having the same conversations <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ] </span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:8px\"><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">&lt;signature&gt; something witty &lt;/signature&gt;</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/302-nazfool","name":"Nazfool","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar302_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"753"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-16T13:05:42-07:00","id":170986,"title":"","content":"Nazfool says it best. I loved The Sea of Shadows, and it answered a ton of questions I had, but if I'm honest the Tempest still gives me headaches. But then I guess it's meant to. As for Wraith 20, Rich Dansky did mention something about maps, which'll be cool.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I had a conscience once. Alas, I appear to have misplaced it.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1309-andreas-rayne","name":"Andreas Rayne","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-16T14:48:14-07:00","id":171056,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Andreas Rayne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/163581-the-sea-of-shadows-prior-3rd-maelstrom?p=170986#post170986\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nazfool says it best. I loved The Sea of Shadows, and it answered a ton of questions I had, but if I'm honest the Tempest still gives me headaches. But then I guess it's meant to. As for Wraith 20, Rich Dansky did mention something about maps, which'll be cool.</div> </div> </div> </div> <br /> TBH, I think it gives everyone headaches. Personally, I think it comes from the difficulty of conceptualizing fictitious metaphysical abstractions into game mechanics. But, when the Underworld gives you relic lemons, make artifact lemonade.<br /> <br /> My troupe took these necrographic frustrations and integrated them into our stories. Not only do players have a tricky time figuring out where to go, but Wraiths do too. <br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">\u201cIf we take Byway X and head towards Necropolis Y, we should be able to head back towards the Tempest to get to Z.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cCouldn\u2019t we just head towards Z?\u201d</span><br /> <br /> &lt;Outbursts of laughter from the rest of the Circle&gt;<br /> <br /> Chuckling, <span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">\u201cSure. We could ask a leprechaun for directions and ride unicorns fueled by rainbows.\u201d</span> After the laughter winds down, <span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">\u201cSeriously though, shut up and get in the boat.\u201d</span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:8px\"><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">&lt;signature&gt; something witty &lt;/signature&gt;</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/302-nazfool","name":"Nazfool","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar302_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"753"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}